          <p>The bearded dragon is one of the most popular lizard species in the world and one of the calmest lizards to keep. It comes from a large part of Australia — from dry, semi-desert and desert regions. They usually grow to 45–55 cm, with females smaller than males and with a narrower head. Prices start at 6,000 din for standard animals and go up to several tens of thousands of dinars for uniquely colored morphs. It is not on the CITES list — no paperwork is needed.</p>
